# `main` is read-only and sync-only

`main` exists only to track `upstream/main` plus the fork-only tooling that sits
on top of it. Do NOT use it as a working branch.

## Allowed on `main`
- Syncing with upstream — ONLY via the `sync-upstream-main` skill
  (`git merge upstream/main`, never rebase), then `git push origin main`.
- Nothing else by default.

## Forbidden on `main`
- No feature work, bug fixes, refactors, or any code edits.
- No experiments, benchmarks, or server runs launched while checked out on `main`.
- No direct commits, no rebases, no force-pushes, no history rewrites.
- Do NOT advance the remote box to `main` for dev work.

## How to work
- Branch off `main` for any change: `git checkout -b <feature> main`.
- Do all edits, commits, and runs on the feature branch.
- To pull in new upstream commits, run the `sync-upstream-main` skill on `main`,
  then merge `main` into your feature branch (not the other way around).

## Tooling exception
Fork-only tooling (`.cursor/rules/`, `.claude/skills/`, `utilities/`) is the one
category that legitimately lives on `main`. Add/update it with a single explicit
tooling commit only when the user asks; never bundle it with code changes.
